# Lesson 2, new hand: partner opens, you have too little to respond.
title: Too weak to respond
id: L02-28
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3
student: S
board: 28
dealer: W
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AKJ853 AK4    Q6     97
  E  QT     J75    A974   KQ32
  S  7642   Q86    JT53   84
  W  9      T932   K82    AJT65

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1S     = 13+ points, at least four spades
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = Fewer than 6 points
     key: 3 HCP plus 1 for the doubleton is 4. With fewer than 6, pass, even with spade support.
     not 2S: A raise shows 6-9. Did you count 4?
     not *: With fewer than 6 points, what does the lesson say to do?
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Partner opened 1♠, and with only 4 points you passed, even with four
  spades. Partner can't count on you for anything, so the auction ends
  here. North is declarer, because he bid spades first, and so East will
  lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E CK  S C4  W CT  N C7
  2   E CQ  S C8  W C5  N C9
  3   E H5  S H6  W H9  N HK
      note: Dummy has no clubs left, so East switches.
  4   N SA  E ST  S S2  W S9
      note: Declarer draws trumps first.
  5   N SK  E SQ  S S4  W C6
      note: One more round, and the trumps are gone.
  6   N HA  E H7  S H8  W H2
      note: Now the heart winners.
  7   N H4  E HJ  S HQ  W H3
      note: The third heart, to dummy's queen.
  8   S D3  W D2  N DQ  E DA
      note: Only diamonds are left to lose, so declarer gives them up.
  9   E D4  S D5  W DK  N D6
  10  W CA  N S3  E C2  S DT
  11  N SJ  E D7  S S6  W CJ
      note: The rest are trumps, all winners.
  12  N S8  E D9  S S7  W D8
      note: Another trump.
  13  N S5  E C3  S DJ  W HT
      note: 9 tricks: 1♠ made with two overtricks.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: draw trumps, cash the hearts, then give up the
  diamonds.

  1♠ made with two overtricks. Your side had 20 points, well short of the
  25 a game needs, so stopping low was right.
